Rearrange the first inequality:
$\begin{aligned}x+y&\ge 2\\y&\ge -x+2\end{aligned}$
Draw $y=-x+2$ solid and $y=x+2$ dotted. Shade on or above the first line and below the second.
Find their meeting point:
$\begin{aligned}-x+2&=x+2\\2x&=0\\x&=0\\y&=2\end{aligned}$
The lines meet at $(0,2)$. This point is excluded because $y<x+2$ is strict. The region lies between the lines to the right of their intersection.
