Ride counts are non-negative integers. The conditions are $x\ge 0$, $y\ge 0$ and $5x+3y\le 16$.
$\begin{aligned}5x+3y&\le 16\\3y&\le -5x+16\\y&\le -\frac{5}{3}x+\frac{16}{3}\end{aligned}$
Draw all boundaries solid and shade the first-quadrant region on or below the budget line. The intercepts are $(\frac{16}{5},0)$ and $(0,\frac{16}{3})$.
Spending exactly $\$16$ requires an integer point on $5x+3y=16$. Using both rides allows $x=1$ or $x=2$; $x=3$ leaves only $\$1$, insufficient for a boat ride.
For $x=1$, the remaining $\$11$ does not buy a whole number of boat rides. For $x=2$:
$\begin{aligned}5(2)+3y&=16\\3y&=6\\y&=2\end{aligned}$
Maya takes two of each ride: $5(2)+3(2)=16$.
